@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
 <p>So that’s the mission and vision. And our strategy is to, “build and fight” (inspired by Nehemiah 4). When God’s people rebuilt the Jerusalem walls, “each of the builders had his sword strapped at his side while he built” (Neh 4:18). Sword and trowel. Build and fight.</p>
 <p>The reason that we must be doing both is because we live among the ruins of what sin has destroyed and God's enemies, just like in Nehemiah’s day, want to make sure that walls aren’t ever built up again. So we have the challenge of rebuilding personal lives and households and a society broken and marred by sin <em>and</em> we have the challenge of fighting off those who want to keep it broken because they hate God and his ways. We need to be craftsmen and warriors.</p>
 <p>So first let’s talk about being craftsmen and our second question, “How do I build?” How do we build toward making disciples who glorify God in all of life for all of Stillwater?</p>
-<p>Nehemiah is a great example to us.<sup class="fn" id="fnref-1"><a href="#fn-1" aria-label="Footnote 1">1</a></sup></p>
+<p>Nehemiah is a great example to us.<sup class="fn" id="fnref-1"><a aria-label="Footnote 1" href="#fn-1">1</a></sup></p>
 <ol><li>First he set an intention. When he hears that the progress has been set back in Jerusalem, he forms an intention. He has a specific desire, “I want to set the return to the land up for success by getting a wall around the capital so that we can be a distinct people.” If you do not know what you are building or what you are fighting, you’re probably not doing much building or fighting.</li><li>Then he made a plan. He knows what materials he will need and how long it will take. How will he get from Cupbearer in Susa to overseeing wall-building in Jerusalem? He makes a plan to make that happen.</li><li>He prayed for God’s blessing. He knows that unless the LORD builds the house, the builders labor in vain.</li><li>And then he acted courageously. He got started. He stuck his neck out and got to work.</li></ol>
 <p>That’s how you build:</p>
 <ol><li>Set an intention.</li><li>Make a plan.</li><li>Pray for God’s help.</li><li>Get to work.</li></ol>
@@ -90,9 +90,3 @@
 <ol><li>What is the mission and vision of our church? To make disciples who glorify God in all of life for all of Stillwater.</li><li>What does that mission/vision look like in our individual lives? Living a godly personal life, creating a faithful and fruitful household, working in a productive vocation, building up the church, and advocating for righteousness as a citizen.</li><li>What should I build and fight first?</li><li>Older men, build sound, exemplary lives.</li><li>Older women, build young women who love their husbands and children.</li><li>Young women, do your part to build a faithful and fruitful household.</li><li>Young men, build self-controlled, upright, godly lives.</li><li>How do I build and fight?</li><li>Set an intention</li><li>Make a plan</li><li>Pray for God’s help</li><li>Get to work</li></ol>
 <p>Let us pray.</p>
